\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every h in Z[x] of degree at least two with positive leading coefficient and a unit root modulo every positive integer, do $c_h,C_h>0$ exist such that every A subset [N] avoiding the nonzero values h(p) for rational primes p as differences satisfies $|A|<=C_h$ $N^{1-c_h}$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every h in Z[x] of degree at least two with positive leading coefficient and a unit root modulo every positive integer, do $c_h,C_h>0$ exist such that every A subset [N] avoiding the nonzero values h(p) for rational primes p as differences satisfies $|A|<=C_h$ $N^{1-c_h}$?

